      "writtenOn": "2022-04-05T08:12:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve been wondering whether you need the inner_lock here, and in some cases below (not all of them are protected). I guess it\u0027s fine because thread-\u003eee *is* the current thread, and when you do copy it out to another thread in the reply case, you do take the lock?\n\nI wonder if it\u0027d be cleaner to just declare a local binder_extended_error at the start here, and only assign it to thread-\u003eee (under lock) when we leave the function, so future readers don\u0027t have to wonder about the same thing.",
      "range": {
